    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[UniFi Switch 7.0.44]]></title>
        <id>b3433760-115d-4fb0-9799-535bbd1af94f</id>
        <link href="https://community.ui.com/releases/UniFi-Switch-7-0-44/b3433760-115d-4fb0-9799-535bbd1af94f"/>
        <updated>2024-03-14T15:18:20.000Z</updated>
        <summary type="html"><![CDATA[Overview
UniFi Switch 7.0.44 adds support for Global ACL Rules on L3 switches.
Improvements

Added support for Global ACL Rules. This requires Network Application 8.1.113 or newer.
Added a new PoE current-usage screen on the touchscreen.
Added PoE Off state on the touchscreen.
Improved SFP module compatibility.
[USW-Pro-Max] Added support for Port Locating on the touchscreen.
[USW-Enterprise-8-PoE] Improved device stability after config provision.
[USW-Pro-Aggregation] Improved SFP28 link stability for manual speed 25Gbps ports.
[USW-Gen1/USW-Pro] Improved CPU usage when forwarding PTPv2 traffic.
[USW] Increased the maximum number of LAG groups.

Bugfixes

Fixed unexpected log spam related to memory checks.
[USW-Enterprise-24-PoE] Fixed an issue where wireless clients couldn't roam when Restricted by MAC ID is enabled on the port that an AP is connected to.
[USW-Pro-Max] Fixed Etherlighting not working if the port speed is 10Mbps.
[USW-Pro-Max] Fixed an issue where routing to other L3 networks may not work after a reboot.
[USW-Pro-Max] Fixed Port Native VLAN not working when VLAN Magic settings are configured.
[USW-Pro] Fixed occasional device freezes during firmware updates.
[USW-Enterprise-8-PoE] Fixed incorrect STP path cost when STP mode is running.
[USP-PDU-Pro] Fixed not showing power utilization on ports where lower power consumption devices are connected.

Known issues

You might experience slow memory increase on USW-Pro-Max switches, this will be fixed in a upcoming firmware release.

Additional information

Your device built-in display may turn black or unresponsive for ~10 minutes after firmware upgrades to upgrade Touchscreen firmware.
Your device's Etherlighting ports may turn off for ~5 minutes after firmware upgrades to upgrade the Etherlighting firmware.


 
If you encounter any issues with this release, please provide us some details on your setup and include the below information:

Switch model(s)
Previous Switch release version
UniFi Network application version]]></summary>
        <author>
            <name>UI-Glenn</name>
        </author>
    </entry>
